{"id":12016,"date":"2025-04-08T22:09:17","date_gmt":"2025-04-08T22:09:17","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=12016"},"modified":"2025-09-05T16:23:03","modified_gmt":"2025-09-05T16:23:03","slug":"remodeling-hidden-costs","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/remodeling-hidden-costs\/","title":{"rendered":"More Remodeling Hidden Costs (and How to Plan for Them)"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When planning a home remodel, most homeowners focus on the big-ticket items\u2014new cabinets, upgraded appliances, or a luxurious bathroom redesign. However, the reality is that remodeling hidden costs can emerge at every step of the process, potentially derailing your budget. Above all, at Harris &amp; Sons, we understand the challenges of managing these unexpected expenses, which is why we emphasize the importance of comprehensive preconstruction planning. This blog explores remodeling hidden costs and provides actionable strategies to prepare for them.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you are looking for a more in-depth and personal discussion with our team regarding your specific project, feel free to book a hassle free, no obligation 1 on 1 virtual consultation with our Construction Consultant:<a href=\"https:\/\/api.leadconnectorhq.com\/widget\/bookings\/harris-sons-virtual-consultation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"\">&nbsp;<strong>Book a Call.<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXcyEOqqGjVO8wNL00sWJvU_0iZ3WQXm1_XHYePehMk17NbxNQ9BKDOGifJNCDJV4lkKxFGH4q5r_Qj490ghBFdYL7F1kzBdWfXt7OjlExX8vLkeEEVjoOSon82QVAWBVvzz4MC2BQ.png\" alt=\"remodeling hidden costs\" class=\"wp-image-12023\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Common Remodeling Hidden Costs in your Project<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Structural Issues<br><\/strong>Many homeowners are unaware of structural problems lurking behind walls, ceilings, or floors until the remodel begins. Issues such as outdated wiring, plumbing problems, or weakened foundations can add thousands to your project.<br>\u2022 <strong>Fact:<\/strong> According to a report from the National Association of Home Builders (NAHB), unexpected repairs account for 10-15% of total project costs. \u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> A Oregon homeowner remodeling a 1920s bungalow discovered asbestos insulation, adding $5,000 in abatement costs.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Permitting Fees and Delays<br><\/strong>Navigating Oregon&#8217;s permit process can be time-consuming and costly. Failing to obtain the correct permits can lead to fines or project shutdowns.<br>\u2022 <strong>Fact:<\/strong> The City of Oregon charges an average of $500-$2,000 per permit, depending on the project\u2019s scope. (City of Oregon Permit Center)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Material Price Fluctuations<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Supply chain disruptions and market demands can cause material costs to spike unexpectedly.<br>\u2022 <strong>Statistic:<\/strong> In 2021, lumber prices increased by over 300%, affecting budgets nationwide. (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.nar.realtor\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">National Association of Realtors<\/a>)<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Temporary Living Expenses<br><\/strong>Extensive remodels may render parts of your home unlivable, requiring alternative accommodations.<br>\u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> A family in Oregon undergoing a kitchen remodel had to rent an Airbnb for six weeks, costing $4,200.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Design Changes Mid-Project<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Making changes after construction begins can lead to additional labor and material costs.<br>\u2022 <strong>Case Study:<\/strong> A homeowner added custom cabinetry mid-project, increasing their remodel cost by $3,000 and delaying the timeline by three weeks.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Strategies to Plan for Hidden Costs<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Set Aside a Contingency Budget<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Allocate 15-20% of your total budget for unforeseen expenses. This cushion helps you stay on track without sacrificing quality.<br>\u2022 <strong>Pro Tip:<\/strong> For a $50,000 remodel, reserve $7,500-$10,000 as your contingency fund.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Invest in a Detailed Preconstruction Process<br><\/strong>At Harris &amp; Sons, our Oregon Preconstruction Process identifies potential issues before they arise, saving time and money. This includes:\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Comprehensive inspections<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accurate cost estimates<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Clear timelines (Learn more about our Oregon Preconstruction Process here)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Partner with an Experienced Contractor<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Choosing a reliable contractor minimizes risks of unexpected costs. Look for:\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transparent pricing<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Positive reviews<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Proven expertise in your area (Read why homeowners trust Harris &amp; Sons)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Communicate and Document Everything<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>Regular communication with your contractor ensures clarity and reduces the risk of surprises. Document all changes in a written agreement to avoid misunderstandings.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Plan for Temporary Accommodations<\/strong><strong><br><\/strong>If your remodel impacts essential areas like the kitchen or bathroom, include temporary living expenses in your budget.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Role of Transparency in Avoiding Hidden Costs<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Certainly, at Harris &amp; Sons, we prioritize transparency in every project. During our initial consultation, we assess potential risks and provide a detailed breakdown of costs, ensuring you\u2019re fully prepared. This approach has saved our clients thousands of dollars and countless hours of stress.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Case Study Highlight<br>The Smith Family Basement Remodel<\/strong>: During a basement renovation in Portland, we discovered moisture issues that required additional waterproofing. Thanks to our preconstruction inspection, this was identified early, and we adjusted the budget to include $3,800 for repairs without delaying the project.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Why the Oregon Preconstruction Process Matters<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Hidden costs can quickly escalate if not addressed proactively. The Oregon Preconstruction Process offered by Harris &amp; Sons ensures:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>A thorough evaluation of your home\u2019s current condition<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accurate budgeting for labor, materials, and permits<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reduced risks of mid-project surprises<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">By addressing these factors upfront, we create a seamless remodeling experience tailored to your needs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thoughts<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While hidden costs are a reality of home remodeling, they don\u2019t have to derail your dream project. With proper planning, a reliable contractor, and a detailed preconstruction process, you can anticipate and manage unexpected expenses effectively. At Harris &amp; Sons, we\u2019re here to help Oregon  homeowners navigate every step of the remodeling journey with confidence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Ready to get started?<br><\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\">Contact Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> today to schedule your consultation and learn more about the Oregon Preconstruction Process.<br><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us\/\" title=\"\">Get in Touch<\/a> | <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/services\/\" title=\"\">Explore Our Services<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>When planning a home remodel, most homeowners focus on the big-ticket items\u2014new cabinets, upgraded appliances, or a luxurious bathroom redesign. However, the reality is that remodeling hidden costs can emerge at every step of the process, potentially derailing your budget. Above all, at Harris &amp; Sons, we understand the challenges of managing these unexpected expenses, [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":12022,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[36,38,33,39],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-12016","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-general","category-remodel","category-remodeling-tips","category-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12016","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=12016"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12016\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13706,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12016\/revisions\/13706"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=12016"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/